{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872474-what-are-you-most-interesting-vices-and-virtues","id":872474,"title":"What are you most interesting Vices and Virtues ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-23T10:26:20-07:00","id":872474,"title":"What are you most interesting Vices and Virtues ?","content":"I thought I would create this thread for people to put up there most interesting vices and virtues they made for a character or NPC. <br /> <br /> Another reason I did it was because I'm trying to find some interesting vices and virtues for this ex SSR (Special Reconnaissance Regiment) Fractal child<br /> <br /> One vice I thought up for another NPC I made was Carnal<br /> <br /> Character Gets back a point of willpower for giving into a Carnal Desire when they should be doing something else be it drinking till they black out, Having sex with a random stranger or beating the crap out of someone for just talking to you the wrong way. I thought Carnal was better then sexual because Carnal can mean more then just sex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T10:29:11-07:00","id":872477,"title":"","content":"I had a demon who's vice was <b>Punctual</b>.<br /> <br /> His Virtue? <b>Smarmy.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T10:37:21-07:00","id":872485,"title":"","content":"I honestly love curiosity as a vice because of the bad situations you can you self in, all in character. <br /> <br /> In general the seven deadly sind make for great vices but a minor quirky character flaw can provide more depth often in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T10:38:11-07:00","id":872489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872474-what-are-you-most-interesting-vices-and-virtues?p=872477#post872477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a demon who's vice was <b>Punctual</b>.<br /> <br /> His Virtue? <b>Smarmy.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Can you explain Smarmy ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T10:59:23-07:00","id":872509,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Smarmy: ingratiating and wheedling in a way that is regarded as insincere or excessive.<br /> <br /> Here's an article on it: <a href=\"http://gawker.com/on-smarm-1476594977\" target=\"_blank\">On smarm.</a></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T11:01:28-07:00","id":872512,"title":"","content":"I guess someone with Cynical as a Virtue would not believe in free lunches, but in a way that encourages them to look for more down-to-earth and lasting solutions, without falling into flat-out pessimism.<br /> <br /> The opposite of that could be Faith as a Vice: someone who fears the weight of responsibility and takes the guidance of others at face value, someone who believes everything will be fine but can't explain why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-23-2016, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T11:21:32-07:00","id":872532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872474-what-are-you-most-interesting-vices-and-virtues?p=872509#post872509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Smarmy: ingratiating and wheedling in a way that is regarded as insincere or excessive.<br /> <br /> Here's an article on it: <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://gawker.com/on-smarm-1476594977&amp;quot;]On</a> smarm.[/URL]</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div> That's a good article. There's an expression that essentially goes &quot;those who warn you care about you&quot;. Someone who doesn't bother to explain why you're wrong doesn't really care that you might be in harm's way, so they are not your friend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T11:34:18-07:00","id":872546,"title":"","content":"One of my players had &quot;Drama Queen&quot; as a Vice. I thought it was exceedingly clever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T13:45:25-07:00","id":872620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872474-what-are-you-most-interesting-vices-and-virtues?p=872546#post872546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my players had &amp;quot;Drama Queen&amp;quot; as a Vice. I thought it was exceedingly clever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ingenious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T14:31:00-07:00","id":872642,"title":"","content":"I have a Bureau of Investigation Agent from the prohibition era. Whose Virtue is Efficient and the Vice of Loyalty.<br /> He would tackle a task in the simplest and stealthy way possible.<br /> But he has a rigid sense of duty and will preform any task asked of him, always give the benefit of the doubt to his superiors and people close to him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T15:21:26-07:00","id":872673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872474-what-are-you-most-interesting-vices-and-virtues?p=872642#post872642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a Bureau of Investigation Agent from the prohibition era. Whose Virtue is Efficient and the Vice of Loyalty.<br /> He would tackle a task in the simplest and stealthy way possible.<br /> But he has a rigid sense of duty and will preform any task asked of him, always give the benefit of the doubt to his superiors and people close to him.</div> </div> </div> </div> This combination of Virtue and Vice reminded me a lot of Dr. Gears from the SCP Foundation, who is an extremely intelligent and dutiful scientist at the top ranks of the Foundation with an unexplained, almost total lack of any emotions. He is also one of few people in the world who can speak with and know the same information as the nebulous 13 Overseers who run the Foundation. Except that Gears has a second Virtue of Stoic + the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration?p=847629#post847629\"><b>Advanced Virtuous Merit</b></a>, and his Vice is closer to Callous. He'd also have the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1errVia6n-HWTT_V2uE4BAI3qOK5O_RkPP1zK2DB5w3c/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Prodigy Merit</b></a> for Composure and Science, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration?p=844180#post844180\"><b>Advanced Patient</b></a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration?p=851048#post851048\"><b>Epic Indomitable</b></a> and Integrity 10.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T15:33:22-07:00","id":872679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872474-what-are-you-most-interesting-vices-and-virtues?p=872485#post872485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly love curiosity as a vice because of the bad situations you can you self in, all in character.<br /> <br /> In general the seven deadly sind make for great vices but a minor quirky character flaw can provide more depth often in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div> What would Curious as a Virtue be like? An open-mind for knowledge and life stories, with enough wisdom to separate the useful from the trivial or dangerous?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T15:40:02-07:00","id":872684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872474-what-are-you-most-interesting-vices-and-virtues?p=872679#post872679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What would Curious as a Virtue be like? An open-mind for knowledge and life stories, with enough wisdom to separate the useful from the trivial or dangerous?</div> </div> </div> </div>The willingness to pursue knowledge and understand the world is how I'd put it as a virtue. I chilidish open mind that simply want to understand the world. As a vitrue I'd have it more focused and less ADD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T22:09:34-07:00","id":872885,"title":"","content":"Madeline character in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/825300-cod-mage-magnum-opus-actual-play\">Magnum Opus</a> have Virtue as <b>Persistent</b> and Vice as <b>Closed</b>. She is set in her ways ( on last game session she said she would rather kill 400 cultists than leave the town ), but she is very emotionally closed, to many drifting away. Because of her Vice she even pushed away her own brother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-24-2016, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T00:37:08-07:00","id":872948,"title":"","content":"The virtue of <b>overly theatric</b>. The vice of <b>deapan snarker</b>. Together, they make for the greatest character you ever saw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T04:08:54-07:00","id":873011,"title":"","content":"I once made a character whose Virtue was <b>corrupt</b>. Needless to say, they had some issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T09:16:05-07:00","id":876712,"title":"","content":"Combo I was worried will end up being too flat but actually ended up fine was <b>Inquisitive</b> as Virtue, with <b>Nosy/Curious</b> as Vice; basically, someone who will sacrifice a leg and an arm to arrive at truth, but who is also often entertained by sticking their noses into someone else's business for no better reason that to sate their curiosity. Someone who won't back off when threatened by mafia, but also someone who will check out truth behind your embarrassing stories simply for kicks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T19:50:30-07:00","id":877259,"title":"","content":"There was a fictional character who's Vice was described as &quot;He always does the right thing, even when he shouldn't&quot;. The character's sense of right and wrong was defined by a written code, with no consideration for mitigating circumstance or degree of sin. For example a thief is a thief, no one cares if he stole bread for his starving children or food from starving children the punishment is the same.<br /> \u200bOn the other end there is the Robin Hood character who does wrong for the greater good, at least as he sees it.<br /> Personally I like the idea of Virtue and Vice being two sides of the same coin, it makes it easier for a normally virtuous character to engage his Vice. One of my players used Ambition, on the one hand it represented the drive to work hard and put themselves out to achieve great things. On the other it represented a willingness to engage in questionable acts to advance their agenda.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T21:07:15-07:00","id":877296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872474-what-are-you-most-interesting-vices-and-virtues?p=877259#post877259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a fictional character who's Vice was described as &amp;quot;He always does the right thing, even when he shouldn't&amp;quot;. The character's sense of right and wrong was defined by a written code, with no consideration for mitigating circumstance or degree of sin. For example a thief is a thief, no one cares if he stole bread for his starving children or food from starving children the punishment is the same.<br /> \u200bOn the other end there is the Robin Hood character who does wrong for the greater good, at least as he sees it.<br /> Personally I like the idea of Virtue and Vice being two sides of the same coin, it makes it easier for a normally virtuous character to engage his Vice. One of my players used Ambition, on the one hand it represented the drive to work hard and put themselves out to achieve great things. On the other it represented a willingness to engage in questionable acts to advance their agenda.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's how I see it as well. The unusual Virtues and Vices that are common among Demons aren't really a sign of a very alien mindset. As I see it, this is caused by the remaining pieces of the G-M's programming and the radical shifts in perspective that accompany the Fall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T23:31:56-07:00","id":877391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872474-what-are-you-most-interesting-vices-and-virtues?p=872673#post872673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This combination of Virtue and Vice reminded me a lot of Dr. Gears from the SCP Foundation, who is an extremely intelligent and dutiful scientist at the top ranks of the Foundation with an unexplained, almost total lack of any emotions. He is also one of few people in the world who can speak with and know the same information as the nebulous 13 Overseers who run the Foundation. Except that Gears has a second Virtue of Stoic + the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration?p=847629#post847629\"><b>Advanced Virtuous Merit</b></a>, and his Vice is closer to Callous. He'd also have the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1errVia6n-HWTT_V2uE4BAI3qOK5O_RkPP1zK2DB5w3c/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Prodigy Merit</b></a> for Composure and Science, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration?p=844180#post844180\"><b>Advanced Patient</b></a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/843870-advanced-merits-homebrew-collaboration?p=851048#post851048\"><b>Epic Indomitable</b></a> and Integrity 10.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've noticed you have a marked tendency to overstat fictional characters - Gears would get away with just Efficient/Callous as Virtue and Vice, <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/supporting-cast-mage-the-awakening/\" target=\"_blank\">Deadpan</a>, and a high Integrity (not necessarily a 10, though). Heck, he's playable as a starting character (<i>every single researcher</i> for the SCP foundation is within the reach of a starting character, other than Dr. Clef (and that's debatable as well - he might just be a Stigmatic with <i>very</i> competitive Supernatural merit choices - his Stigmata being his big ol' spider head)).<br /> <br /> More on topic:<br /> <br /> Kind as a Vice (be nice to people <i>even when it's not a good idea</i>).<br /> Polite as a Virtue (&quot;I say, Reginald, that pack of Werewolves has put us in a spot of bother! Still, no need to swear like that, I say!&quot;)<br /> Murder as a Virtue (Oh, Mortal Remains, why do you say such wonderful things?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T01:04:56-07:00","id":877449,"title":"","content":"Kind as a Vice? Have it come across as patronizing and it would work. There were those who justified all sorts of oppression under the guise of 'helping', especially their inferiors.<br /> The Gentleman Villain is a Bond staple. &quot;No Mr. Bond, I want you to die.&quot;<br /> Murder for a purpose, in service of a greater cause. &quot;That is a sacrifice I am willing to make.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bCorruption as a Virtue? Played out as a revolutionary fighting the man. &quot;We are fighting that greatest of evils, taxes.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T05:42:33-07:00","id":877598,"title":"","content":"What could be the difference between Humorous as a Virtue and a Vice? Would the Joker fit into either category?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T06:06:35-07:00","id":877610,"title":"","content":"Humorous Virtue is about using humour to bring the light to the world, make others and yourself smiling while fighting the good fight. Humorous Vice is about escapism and using jokes to forget about your everyday pain, to look away from the body in front of you and crack a joke to cling to your sanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T06:12:14-07:00","id":877617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872474-what-are-you-most-interesting-vices-and-virtues?p=877610#post877610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humorous Virtue is about using humour to bring the light to the world, make others and yourself smiling while fighting the good fight. Humorous Vice is about escapism and using jokes to forget about your everyday pain, to look away from the body in front of you and crack a joke to cling to your sanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>They both comes to me as archetypal <b>Vampire: Masquerade </b>2ED corebook Malkavian character - you know, neurotic comic...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T17:32:07-07:00","id":879792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.foreignercn.com/index.php?option=com_content&amp;id=5047:the-five-constant-virtues-of-china&amp;catid=1:history-and-culture&amp;Itemid=114\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://www.foreignercn.com/templates/ja_xenia_ii/images/logo-blue.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.foreignercn.com/index.php?option=com_content&amp;id=5047:the-five-constant-virtues-of-china&amp;catid=1:history-and-culture&amp;Itemid=114\" target=\"_blank\"> The Five Constant Virtues of China </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.foreignercn.com/index.php?option=com_content&amp;id=5047:the-five-constant-virtues-of-china&amp;catid=1:history-and-culture&amp;Itemid=114\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.foreignercn.com/index.php?option=com_content&amp;id=5047:the-five-constant-virtues-of-china&amp;catid=1:history-and-culture&amp;Itemid=114 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Owning over thousands of years of history, the Chinese have created a brilliant history and culture, and at the same time have formed their own moral code that has played an important role in social development and progress. This is what we call Traditional Virtues (chu&aacute;n t\u01d2ng m\u011bi d&eacute; \u4f20\u7edf\u7f8e\u5fb7), which still have great significance today and whose value to the development of human civilization is now widely recognized. </div> </div> </div><br /> If anyone needs some inspiration, here is something cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T17:52:58-07:00","id":879804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872474-what-are-you-most-interesting-vices-and-virtues?p=877598#post877598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What could be the difference between Humorous as a Virtue and a Vice? Would the Joker fit into either category?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Joker's vice is &quot;wrath&quot; of some sort, he has a very short temper, and you can see that he's a bit out of control at those points. Not sure on his virtue, is entropy a virtue?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T19:35:55-07:00","id":879852,"title":"","content":"Freedom of Expression, damn the consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T09:56:11-07:00","id":880241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872474-what-are-you-most-interesting-vices-and-virtues?p=877598#post877598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What could be the difference between Humorous as a Virtue and a Vice? Would the Joker fit into either category?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a Mask/Batman crossover where Joker gets the mask. By the end of the story he's hijacked a tv network to broadcast his new brand of pandering, goofy, lowest-common-denominator entertainment (the more crazy brutal stuff didn't test well).<br /> <br /> Leaving alone that suppression isn't exactly Vice, and it's a crossover, and the fact that his motivations are notoriously fickle, Joker's Virtue and Vice both being <i>Anything </i>For A Laugh* sounds pretty solid.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">*for a given value of &quot;laughter&quot;, of course</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T13:12:55-07:00","id":881205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872474-what-are-you-most-interesting-vices-and-virtues?p=873011#post873011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I once made a character whose Virtue was <b>corrupt</b>. Needless to say, they had some issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you saying their vice is Vice itself? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T13:24:26-07:00","id":881213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872474-what-are-you-most-interesting-vices-and-virtues?p=881205#post881205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you saying their vice is Vice itself? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Slightly more complete context of their vice and virtue:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Vice:</b> Detached. The world is a bitter pill to swallow. Wash it down with water, gulp it down without tasting it, maybe it'll become a bit more bearable.<br /> <b>Virtue</b>: Corrupt. Systems can't protect everyone, only those that can use them. If you want to achieve anything, you need be one of those people, and know what makes the gears turn. Make the clock ring at the times you set. </div> </div> </div>Take whatever conclusions you will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 05-03-2016, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T15:23:13-07:00","id":884945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872474-what-are-you-most-interesting-vices-and-virtues?p=881213#post881213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Slightly more complete context of their vice and virtue:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Vice:</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Detached. The world is a bitter pill to swallow. Wash it down with water, gulp it down without tasting it, maybe it'll become a bit more bearable.</span></i></span></span><br /> <b>Virtue</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i><span style=\"font-size:13px\">: Corrupt. Systems can't protect everyone, only those that can use them. If you want to achieve anything, you need be one of those people, and know what makes the gears turn. Make the clock ring at the times you set.</span></i></span></span> </div> </div> </div>Take whatever conclusions you will.</div> </div> </div> </div> It sounds like you could describe their Virtue as Pragmatic if you wanted to be generous, and their Vice as Defeatist if you wanted to be harsh.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T09:05:20-07:00","id":885411,"title":"","content":"When I wrote up Root from Person of Interest as a Demon, I gave her the Virtue Ruthless, and the Vice Compassionate - as her compassion is the part of herself she tries to repress, while her ruthlessness she proudly cultivated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T02:25:49-08:00","id":1031505,"title":"","content":"Anymore good ones ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T06:01:27-08:00","id":1035692,"title":"","content":"I like it when the vice and virtue are the exact same thing, as it adds depth to that facet of a person. <br /> <br /> Example Perfectionist as both virtue and vice, when the Perfectionism leads to excellent achievement it acts as a virtue, when it gets out of hand it acts like a vice.<br /> <br /> Another virtue/vice flirt, when used to bring joy and fun and playful its a virtue, when used to manipulate for selfish destructive ends or provoke jeaolousy on purpose its a vice.<br /> <br /> Zeal virtue when channeling that passion to create good in the world, vice when it devovles into acts of a Zealot. <br /> <br /> Honesty virtue when you tell people what they need to hear, vice when you use it as an excuse to be hurtful for no benifit to the hurt person.<br /> <br /> Lust is a virtue when your respsonible in it presuit, taking and giving pleasure with another person, it becomes a vice when you actively choose to ignore consquences you know will happen just to appease your lust.<br /> <br /> Hatred virtue when acting against what you hate if its sonething really bad like hating murderers, vice when you act on your hatred in a way that causes innocent people to suffer for it, like getting an innocent person convicted for murder that if you hadn't been think with hatred, you'd have know was innocent. <br /> <br /> Hope, virtue when you give hope to those who have given up and they pull it together, vice when you give someone false hope. <br /> <br /> Justice virtue when you help someone achieve justice, vice when you violate someones legal rights to achieve it.<br /> <br /> Sadism virtue when done in a consentual kinky way that gives pleasure,vice when you get careless and someone gets injured.<br /> <br /> Controlling, good when you take charge of a chaotic situation and show leadership, vice when your being manipulative and you know the other person resents it.<br /> <br /> Logical, virtue when your making rational decisions, vice when you use it to maintain an emotional distance from those that care about you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 01-21-2017, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T14:38:16-08:00","id":1035841,"title":"","content":"Got a Mage player right now who took Virtue: Perspective (she draws strength from taking the long view), Vice: Polite (her social front is an easy way to escape problems)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T10:20:35-08:00","id":1036147,"title":"","content":"One from a demon, but mostly characters from other media<br /> <br /> Virtue: Perfectionist (OCD for a slightly different take)<br /> Vice: Curious<br /> An angel thought it figured out what the GM was doing, and realized the GM's calculations were WRONG! So, send one more human into the mill to fix the math. Oops, fall. Maybe the GM made a 0-index/ 1-index array error <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> From In Nomine, there is a demon &quot;Kobol, the Prince of Dark Humor&quot;. I think that kind of humor is of the 'make the mortal realize how futile and illusionary is life, so they suicide' variety. Note: IANAComedian. <br /> <br /> Seven Deadly Sins anime:<br /> Melodias Vice: Devious. His cunning plans may work, but have lots of collateral damage.<br /> Gowther: Virtue Curious. Vice Curious. Helps people get memories back, will try to understand even a monster. But, will mention other people's secrets at really inappropriate times, and look in your head without asking first.<br /> <br /> One Piece anime<br /> Sanji Virtue: Miserly, Vice: Kind. Goes to extremes to keep everyone fed while conserving food. But will feed anyone, including people who are obviously going to do evil things after. I don't know where 'beating up people who waste food' goes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T10:27:07-08:00","id":1036154,"title":"","content":"definitely miserly. Although I wonder if &quot;Chivalrous&quot; could be his virtue","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T11:24:35-08:00","id":1036185,"title":"","content":"In my Hunter game, one of the PCs had Vice: Douche. He regained a lot of Willpower...<br /> <br /> The character was still a team player, and genuinely useful, but he was always doing little things that pissed people off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3934-fetch","name":"Fetch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3934_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T10:24:48-08:00","id":1036697,"title":"","content":"I had a Demon that I played a game with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar576_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"576\" data-vbnamecard=\"576\">Ephsy</a> with that is still has my most fun virtue/vice combination that I've ever played:<br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Creative<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Obedience <br /> <br /> My character, Ms. Spindle valued creativity as most high in that's how a task can be done efficiently. But at the end of the day she regrets that she had to fall as Obedience is still core and comfortable to her. Her cover was that of a child which catered nicely to her vice. I liked it because to Ms. Spindle, doing what her Cover's parents told her to do was as much of a vice to her as smoking was to some grisled Hunter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T18:48:51-08:00","id":1037557,"title":"","content":"One character of mine started off with the Ambitious Virtue as a mortal, but after her first death (Sin-Eater) it shifted and became the Driven Vice. The real issue was that her goal as a mortal involved learning about a certain type of supernatural being. She hadn't reached it yet when she became a supernatural herself. She still wants the answers she was looking for, except now she also has her own supernatural issues to deal with, and in some ways it's even more dangerous to investigate other splats than when she was a mortal.<br /> <br /> <b>Ambitious (Premortem Virtue, from the revised rulebook):</b> Your character has goals she wants to accomplish and the drive to achieve them. In some people who don\u2019t deserve the accolades they seek, ambition is a Vice \u2014 for her it\u2019s a guiding mission. Regain Willpower when your character puts herself at risk for the sake of following her long-term goal.<br /> <b>Driven (Postmortem Vice):</b> Your character has one eye fixed on a certain objective and is hard-pressed to let go when an opportunity arises to pursue it. Regain Willpower when your character pursues her own goals at the cost of other, more pressing matters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/2.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":12708,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12708-chesh","user":"Chesh","date":". 01-24-2017, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12708-chesh","name":"Chesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12708_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T06:46:23-08:00","id":1165563,"title":"","content":"i don't know if this thread is still active but i have a obrimos mage that has trustworthy as a virtue and his vice is ambitious. i don't know what to do with that but so far he's good at keeping secrets but can be overacheiveing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23562-fruity20","name":"fruity20","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T10:10:47-08:00","id":1165609,"title":"","content":"Ambition or ambitious has popped up at least twice in the thread already.<br /> <br /> There was an old comic line called Scion, and an ongoing called the First, within it. The First were gods, sort of a backwards interpretation of Chronicles' spirits. They came first and represent things like Greed and Wisdom and other concepts and attributes, with their children the Second representing more complex meshes of the virtues or vices. They lived on some floating islands separated by a vast gulf and most people couldn't cross it. One side had the 'good' First, honor and prudence and so forth, the other had the 'bad' first, like greed and recklessness. If you ended up having a child that belonged on the other island they would be sent there shortly after birth.<br /> <br /> I mention this because there were rare First and Seconds who could cross the gulf between lands. One of them was Ambition (I forget his character's name). The idea of it being depicted as both a driven but virtuous attribute, as well as a base and negative attribute has played out before. It's something that happens, like most things, it's not objectively bad or good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T10:50:49-08:00","id":1165623,"title":"","content":"Virtue: Precise<br /> Vice: Hope<br /> <br /> Gonna need to wait a bit before elaborating on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T18:29:16-08:00","id":1165727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fruity20</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872474-what-are-you-most-interesting-vices-and-virtues?p=1165563#post1165563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i don't know if this thread is still active but i have a obrimos mage that has trustworthy as a virtue and his vice is ambitious. i don't know what to do with that but so far he's good at keeping secrets but can be overacheiveing.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSounds like someone just begging to join a conspiracy. He keeps his promises and commitments but his motivation is personal aggrandizement, not ethics. The society only advances you if they trust you won't tell where the bodies are buried.<br /> \u200bI would call this a good example of how even Virtues can fall into the gray.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T02:41:04-08:00","id":1165797,"title":"","content":"Virtue: Smarmy<br /> Vice: Smartass","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-26T22:49:04-07:00","id":1449761,"title":"","content":"I have not posted in here for a bit but here is a list for you guys <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><u><b>Huge List Of Virtues</b></u></span><br /> Ready, set, virtues!<ul><li><b>A</b><ul><li><b>Ability</b> - a quality that permits or facilitates achievement or accomplishment</li> <li><b>Acceptance</b> - a disposition to tolerate or accept people or situations</li> <li><b>Acuity</b> - keenness of hearing, sight, or intellect</li> <li><b>Affability</b> - good-natured, friendly, and easy to talk to</li> <li><b>Altruism</b> - the quality of unselfish concern for the welfare of others</li> <li><b>Appreciation</b> - understanding of the nature or meaning or quality or magnitude of something</li> <li><b>Assiduousness</b> - showing persistent and hard-working effort in doing something</li> <li><b>Assertiveness</b> - aggressive self-assurance; given to making bold assertions</li> <li><b>Attentiveness</b> - the trait of being observant and paying attention</li> <li><b>Autonomy</b> - immunity from arbitrary exercise of authority; political independence</li> <li><b>Awareness</b> - the ability to perceive, to feel, or to be conscious of events, objects or patterns</li> </ul></li> <li><b>B</b><ul><li><b>Balance</b> - the ability to remain poised; to give equal attention to all things; to be fair</li> <li><b>Beauty</b> - the qualities that give pleasure to the senses</li> <li><b>Benevolence</b> - an inclination to do kind or charitable acts</li> </ul></li> <li><b>C</b><ul><li><b>Candor</b> - the ability to make judgments free from discrimination or dishonesty</li> <li><b>Caring</b> - feeling and exhibiting concern and empathy for others</li> <li><b>Caution</b> - judiciousness in avoiding harm or danger</li> <li><b>Charity</b> - a kindly and lenient attitude toward people</li> <li><b>Chastity</b> - abstaining from sexual relations</li> <li><b>Cleanliness</b> - the habit of keeping free of superficial imperfections</li> <li><b>Commitment</b> - the trait of sincere and steadfast fixity of purpose</li> <li><b>Compassion</b> - the humane quality of understanding the suffering of others and wanting to do something about it</li> <li><b>Confidence</b> - freedom from doubt; belief in yourself and your abilities</li> <li><b>Conscientiousness</b> - the trait of being painstaking and careful</li> <li><b>Consideration</b> - the process of giving careful thought to something</li> <li><b>Contentment</b> - happiness with one\u2019s situation in life</li> <li><b>Cooperativeness</b> - amenability: the trait of working well with others</li> <li><b>Courage</b> - a quality of spirit that enables you to face danger or pain without showing fear</li> <li><b>Courteousness</b> - exhibiting politeness and gracious good manners</li> <li><b>Creativity</b> - a mental and social process involving the generation of new ideas or concepts</li> <li><b>Curiosity</b> - a state in which you want to learn more about something</li> </ul></li> <li><b>D</b><ul><li><b>Daring</b> - courage combined with a willingness to take risks or attempt difficult or unconventional things</li> <li><b>Dauntlessness</b> - resolute courageousness; not to be daunted or intimidated; fearless; intrepid; bold</li> <li><b>Dependability</b> - worthy of reliance or trust; consistent in performance or behavior</li> <li><b>Detachment</b> - cool-headed withdrawal; avoiding emotional involvement</li> <li><b>Determination</b> - the quality of being driven to do or achieve something; firmness of purpose</li> <li><b>Diligence</b> - conscientiousness in paying proper attention to a task; giving the degree of care required in a given situation</li> <li><b>Discernment</b> - understanding; the mental ability to discriminate between like things</li> <li><b>Discretion</b> - knowing how to avoid embarrassment or distress</li> <li><b>Dutifulness</b> - piety by virtue of devotion; the willingness to be obedient out of a sense of moral obligation and/or respect</li> </ul></li> <li><b>E</b><ul><li><b>Empathy</b> - understanding and entering into another\u2019s feelings</li> <li><b>Encouragement</b> - the expression of approval and support</li> <li><b>Endurance</b> - the power to withstand hardship or stress</li> <li><b>Enthusiasm</b> - exuberance; overflowing with eager enjoyment or approval</li> <li><b>Equanimity</b> - composure; steadiness of mind under stress</li> <li><b>Equity</b> - conformity to rules or standards</li> <li><b>Erudite</b> - characterized by great knowledge; learne