assion for the suffering of others</li> <li><b>Pomposity</b> - an excessive sense of self-importance, usually displayed through exaggerated seriousness or stateliness in speech and manner</li> <li><b>Pride</b> - a haughty attitude shown by somebody who believes, often unjustifiably, that he or she is better than others</li> <li><b>Prejudice</b> - an unfounded hatred, fear, or mistrust of a person or group, especially one of a particular religion, ethnicity, nationality, sexual preference, or social status</li> <li><b>Preposterousness</b> - going very much against what is thought to be sensible or reasonable</li> <li><b>Pretentiousness</b> - acting as though more important or special than is warranted, or appearing to have an unrealistically high self-image</li> <li><b>Profligacy</b> - extremely extravagant or wasteful</li> <li><b>Promiscuity</b> - behavior characterized by casual and indiscriminate sexual intercourse, often with many people</li> </ul></li> <li><b>R</b><ul><li><b>Rage</b> - sudden and extreme anger</li> <li><b>Rashness</b> - acting with, resulting from, or characteristic of thoughtless, impetuous behavior</li> <li><b>Recklessness</b> - marked by a lack of thought about danger or other possible undesirable consequences</li> <li><b>Resentfulness</b> - annoyed or bitter about having been badly treated, or characterized by such a feeling of annoyance</li> <li><b>Rowdiness</b> - a rough and noisy person who often causes disturbances</li> <li><b>Rudeness</b> - disagreeable or discourteous in manner or action; offensive to accepted standards of decency</li> <li><b>Ruthlessness</b> - having or showing no pity or mercy</li> </ul></li> <li><b>S</b><ul><li><b>Secrecy</b> - unwillingness to reveal information</li> <li><b>Self-importance</b> - an unrealistically high evaluation of your own importance or worth</li> <li><b>Self-indulgence</b> - lack of self-control in pursuing your own pleasure or satisfaction</li> <li><b>Self-pity</b> - the self-indulgent belief that your life is harder and sadder than everyone else\u2019s</li> <li><b>Selfishness</b> - concerned with your own interests, needs, and wishes while ignoring those of others</li> <li><b>Senselessness</b> - apparently or really without purpose or meaning; demonstrating a lack of reason and intelligence</li> <li><b>Short-Sightedness</b> - doing or determining without taking the future into account</li> <li><b>Sloth</b> - a dislike of work or any kind of physical exertion</li> <li><b>Snobbishness</b> - displaying an offensively superior condescending manner</li> <li><b>Spite</b> - a malicious, usually small-minded desire to harm or humiliate somebody</li> <li><b>Stingy</b> - not generous in giving or spending money</li> <li><b>Stubbornness</b> - unreasonably and obstructively determined to persevere or prevail</li> <li><b>Sulkiness</b> - a sullen moody resentful disposition; in a bad mood and refusing to communicate because of resentment for a real or imagined grievance</li> <li><b>Sullenness</b> - dourly disposition; showing bad temper or hostility by a refusal to talk, behave sociably, or cooperate cheerfully</li> </ul></li> <li><b>T</b><ul><li><b>Tetchiness</b> - oversensitive and easily upset or annoyed</li> <li><b>Thieving</b> - to steal something, or steal things</li> <li><b>Thoughtlessness</b> - showing a lack of planning or forethought; showing a lack of consideration for other people or for consequences</li> <li><b>Treasonous</b> - one willing to betray the allegiance owed by somebody to his or her own country</li> <li><b>Triteness</b> - one who overuses common phrases or conversation topics and consequently makes them lack in interest or originality</li> <li><b>Tricky</b> - likely to cheat or outwit somebody</li> <li><b>Twisted</b> - morally unacceptable; badly affected by unpleasant experiences or constant disappointment</li> </ul></li> <li><b>U</b><ul><li><b>Unfaithfulness</b> - engaging in sexual relations with somebody other than a spouse or partner; untrue to commitments, duties, beliefs, or ideals</li> <li><b>Unloving</b> - not giving or reciprocating affection</li> <li><b>Untrustworthiness</b> - the trait of not deserving trust or confidence</li> </ul></li> <li><b>V</b><ul><li><b>Vainglory</b> - excessive pride in or boastfulness about personal abilities or achievements</li> <li><b>Vanity</b> - excessive pride, especially in personal appearance</li> <li><b>Vengeful</b> - having or showing a strong desire for revenge</li> <li><b>Voracity</b> - unusually eager or enthusiastic about an activity</li> </ul></li> <li><b>W</b><ul><li><b>Wastefulness</b> - using resources unwisely</li> <li><b>Weakness</b> - lack of strength, power, or determination</li> <li><b>Wildness</b> - overwhelmed by a strong emotion such as anger, grief, or desire; not tame; living or having lived in the wilderness</li> <li><b>Wrath</b> - strong anger, often with a desire for revenge</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Z</b><ul><li><b>Zealousness</b> - actively and unreservedly enthusiastic to the point of fervor</li> </ul></li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-29T20:26:44-07:00","id":1450263,"title":"","content":"I know virtues and vices are supposed to be single words that serve as shorthand for a character's defining ideal and character flaw, but the most interesting personality I played was something that came into being over the course of a game. It didn't quite fit the virtue and vice I picked initially and I never figured out quite the right words to sum it up.<br /> <br /> My character was bitten in the middle of a zombie siege on an isolated cabin in the woods. Real standard tropey horror movie stuff, but what was not standard was that through some insanely good rolls he survived long enough to be cured and went on to participate in a sequel chronicle.<br /> <br /> But between the bite and the cure there was a stretch where in and out of character I wrestled with the specter of a terminal illness and the absolute certainty that he had at most a few days to live. And there I found a weird sort of clarity, an understanding of the self preservation instinct as a sort of shackles that he was now free of. He was, in effect, already dead and that meant he didn't have to waste any thought or effort on his own survival. No question on who would go into the basement first, send the dead guy! Any subsequent bites won't matter! He could take all of the necessary risks because for him there was nothing left to lose, it was already lost, and further risk was meaningless!<br /> <br /> It wasn't quite suicidal, because he considered himself an asset to everyone else's survival and was damned determined to milk his failing body for its maximum utility. It was however, a profoundly strange lack of self regard, lack of self care. A weirdly third person utilitarian view that said &quot;Don't waste any resources on yourself because you're dying soon anyway, give it to those who might yet live.&quot;<br /> <br /> And then... he lived, except he wasn't really living because the fatalism had worked so well that he never left that mindset behind. He wasn't living he was just... failing to die, indefinitely. The lack of self regard became a vice as he allowed himself to suffer ongoing emotional trauma on the theory that you never have to deal with the consequences if you just die first. At the same time, it also fueled his virtue as he poured all of that displaced energy into trying to solve the problems of everyone around him before he burnt out for good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T12:11:50-07:00","id":1450336,"title":"","content":"A changeling wendigo character that was pensive and nervous, self-conscious to the extreme, but with this incredibly deep well of passion and love and anger. Virtue: cautious, Vice: hungry (in the metaphorical and literal sense).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26844-quixote","name":"Quixote","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}